@node "Disc"
@toc "Disc"

              5D-AdiMenu was first designed as a Doormenu....

        But it works in a quite strange way, which lets 5D-AdiMenu
             act like some kind of ~SS_ - replacement... hehe

    Well You can define Textfiles like Commands now, and in this case,
  You can give them Access-levels and Multi- or Single-command options, 
                           like in normal doors!


                             @{" HALLELUJA! " link "MAIN"}

@endnode

@node "Req" "Requirements"
@toc "Req"

       Any Amiga (500,600,1000,1200,2000,3000,4000,4000T,5000(?)....
it should also run on a Sinclair ZX81, but i hadn`t got the  chance to test!
                   Installed S-Express, /X 2.xx or 3.xx
                           Some bottles of Bluna
                       A dead cat (black preferred)
                        Some chilpi-wongo-wacklers
                   Some nights playing Gravity Force II

                            @{" BACK TO MAIN MENU? " link "MAIN"}

@endnode
@node "Inst" "Installing 5D-AdiMenu V1.0"
@toc "Inst"

Just copy the files

                   5D-AdiMenu
                   5D-AdiMUI.Guide

          and the drawer

                   @{"TEXT" link "TEXT"}

                   to DOORS:5D-AdiMenu/

-------------------------------------------------------
/X 2.xx or S-Express:

Copy the drawer 5D-AdiMenu to DOORS:

Edit Your BBS.CMD and snap in the following:

*Nameofdoor      XM001DOORS:5D-AdiMenu/5D-AdiMenu
-------------------------------------------------------
/X 3.xx:

Copy the drawer 5D-AdiMenu to DOORS:

Just create an icon and copy it to Your SYSCMD-Directory
(see the examples inside the archive!!!!)

                            @{" BACK TO MAIN MENU? " link "MAIN"}
@endnode
@node "What" "---> What it does: <---"
@toc "What"

        5D-AdiMenu reads the Commandline, which means it looks for
       the command it was launched with... Well it`s simple, I just
     can`t explain how it works, but it`s quite simple.... so... try 
             it out.. sorry.... a well.. let`s have a drink...

                            @{" YES !" link "MAIN"}
@endnode
@node "TEXT" "drawer TEXT"
@toc "TEXT"

    In the drawer DOORS:5D-ADIMENU/TEXT, there are all those Textfiles,
                     You assigned the commands to....
 
    E.G. if You have a command called "DOORS", the textfile You want to
               display must be DOORS:5D-ADIMENU/TEXT/DOORS .
   This Textfile can contain ANSI-Codes, MCI-messages, Screenclearers or
                  whatever You want (even Ketchup!).... 

                          @{" Hummhumm " link "Inst"}
@endnode
